@startuml Outbox - O Problema (dual-write)
title Dual-write - banco e broker nao sao atomicos

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor #121212
skinparam defaultFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam titleFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam ArrowColor #E3E3E8
skinparam ArrowFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam queue {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #8A8A8F
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}

component "ecommerce" as EC
database "Postgres\n(orders, order_saga)" as DB
queue "RabbitMQ" as RMQ

EC --> DB : 1. grava estado (commit)
EC --> RMQ : 2. publica evento

note bottom of EC
  Sem transacao comum entre os dois.
  Falha entre 1 e 2:
  - gravou e nao publicou: evento perdido
  - publicou e nao gravou: evento fantasma
end note

@enduml


@startuml Outbox - A Solucao (fluxo)
title Outbox - uma escrita so no banco, relay publica depois

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam backgroundColor #121212
skinparam defaultFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam titleFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam queue {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #E3E3E8
  ArrowFontColor #E3E3E8
  LifeLineBorderColor #8A8A8F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  ParticipantBorderColor #E3E3E8
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  ParticipantFontColor #E3E3E8
  DatabaseBorderColor #E3E3E8
  DatabaseBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  DatabaseFontColor #E3E3E8
  QueueBorderColor #E3E3E8
  QueueBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  QueueFontColor #E3E3E8
  GroupBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  GroupBorderColor #8A8A8F
  GroupFontColor #E3E3E8
  GroupHeaderFontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #8A8A8F
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}

participant "ecommerce\n(request)" as API
database "Postgres" as DB
participant "Outbox Relay" as REL
queue "RabbitMQ" as RMQ

group 1 transacao so
  API -> DB : INSERT order + saga + outbox
  API -> DB : COMMIT
end
note over API, DB
  Ou tudo commita junto, ou nada.
  Acabou o dual-write.
end note

== background ==

REL -> DB : SELECT pendentes\nFOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
REL -> RMQ : publica evento
REL -> DB : UPDATE outbox SET published_at

note over REL, RMQ
  Relay roda em intervalo.
  Entrega at-least-once:
  pode repetir, consumidor desduplica (inbox).
end note

@enduml


@startuml Outbox - Relay e Idempotencia
title Outbox - entrega at-least-once e inbox no consumo

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam backgroundColor #121212
skinparam defaultFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam titleFontColor #E3E3E8
skinparam queue {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #E3E3E8
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #E3E3E8
  ArrowFontColor #E3E3E8
  LifeLineBorderColor #8A8A8F
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  ParticipantBorderColor #E3E3E8
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  ParticipantFontColor #E3E3E8
  DatabaseBorderColor #E3E3E8
  DatabaseBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  DatabaseFontColor #E3E3E8
  QueueBorderColor #E3E3E8
  QueueBackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  QueueFontColor #E3E3E8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #2A2A2E
  BorderColor #8A8A8F
  FontColor #E3E3E8
}

participant "Outbox Relay" as REL
database "Postgres\n(outbox)" as DB
queue "RabbitMQ" as RMQ
participant "Consumidor\n(payment / inventory)" as CON
database "Postgres\n(inbox)" as IN

REL -> DB : reserva lote (SKIP LOCKED)
REL -> RMQ : publica evento [event_id]
RMQ -> CON : entrega evento
CON -> IN : INSERT event_id\nON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
alt event_id novo
  CON -> CON : processa o evento
else event_id ja visto
  CON -> CON : ignora (duplicata)
end

note over REL, DB
  Se cair apos publicar e antes de
  marcar published_at, republica.
  Por isso o consumo precisa ser idempotente.
end note

@enduml
